From b79fa1e2638460ee40b3a9a0bfd08ddec9f2fc70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:19:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests/checkasm: add scaler-path packed 4:2:2 packer and
 16-bit hscale coverage

Add check_yuv2packed422_1/2/X to sw_yuv2yuv.c, oracling the scaler-path
yuv2packed1/2/X kernels for yuyv422/uyvy422/yvyu422 (libswscale/output.c's
yuv2422_{1,2,X}_c_template, registered unconditionally for these three
dst formats). These differ from the existing check_packed422 oracle in
this file: that one covers the *unscaled* planar->packed converters,
these cover the general scaler's packed-output path (used whenever an
AltiVec kernel for it exists, gated only by dst format). The context is
built with SWS_BITEXACT so no unscaled special converter intercepts
convert_unscaled, ff_sws_init_scale() is called explicitly to defend
against sws_init_context()'s early-return-on-unscaled-converter path,
and the three pointers are asserted non-NULL. Inputs are kept inside the
C reference's clip window (documented in the new file comment): the
"(Y1|Y2|U|V) & 0x100" clip test only fires, and only then matches true
saturation, when the pre-clip result is in [-256, 511], so _1/_2 use the
full int16 range and _X masks to non-negative 15-bit. Widths, per-line
src offsets and dst byte offsets are swept per combination, comparing
the whole 0x55-filled destination arena so an over/under-run fails too.
Before any AltiVec counterpart exists these are C-only ("no tests to
perform"); verified clean on seeds 1/42/777 plus a --bench listing
showing all 45 new C names driven.

Also extend sw_scale.c's check_hscale to real high-depth source formats
(yuv420p10/yuv420p16) so hScale16To15_c/hScale16To19_c's depth-derived
shift is actually exercised (their C reference reads
c->opts.src_format's pixdesc depth; the previous test only ever built
contexts with the default yuv420p src format regardless of the
srcBpc/dstBpc override). This exposed a latent bug in the existing test
harness: hScale16To15_c/hScale16To19_c dereference c->opts.src_format,
but check_hscale's call_ref/call_new passed a literal NULL for that
argument -- harmless for the 8-bit-src C refs (which never touch it),
but a NULL-pointer segfault once a 16-bit row actually reached that
code path. Fixed by passing the real context throughout (harmless for
the 8-bit rows). Verified: existing 8-bit ALTIVEC hscale rows still
pass, the new 16-bit rows run and pass as C-only (144 new hscale_16_*
names, split evenly across yuv420p10be/yuv420p16be), seeds 1/42/777.

